WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.960
( Theme music playing )

2
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.480
A cripple?

3
00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.120
You let a cripple escape?

4
00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.160
The boy can't walk.

5
00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.040
But somehow he slipped past you?

6
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.440
The giant must have took him.

7
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.600
The giant?

8
00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.160
Hodor?

9
00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.720
Oh. well. that's all right. then.

10
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:29.120
You let a halfwit
Escape with a cripple.

11
00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.880
And Rickon. too? The little one?

12
00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.280
Gone along with the wildling woman.

13
00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.600
The one you were fucking.

14
00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:47.200
( grunting )

15
00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.120
( man groaning )

16
00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:53.640
( panting )

17
00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:59.040
Right. get the horses
And the hounds.

18
00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.360
-( dogs barking )
-Come on. find the scent.

19
00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.120
Come on. where they going?

20
00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.640
Halt!

21
00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:26.360
Enjoying your first hunt?

22
00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:29.560
So far. hunting seems
Very similar to riding. my lord.

23
00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.880
-With hunting.
There's blood at the end.
-They're little boys.

24
00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.960
I was a little boy
When I was torn away from
My home and brought here.

25
00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.560
So I kept my word.

26
00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.480
I never ran away.

27
00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:42.480
If I find them soon enough.
I won't hurt them.

28
00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.440
Well. I'll hurt them.
But I won't kill them.

29
00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.360
Those boys are of far more value
To you alive than dead.

30
00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.240
They have no value to me missing.

31
00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.640
Robb will have sent a force
To retake Winterfell by now.

32
00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.960
Robb's in the Riverlands.
My sister's in Deepwood Motte.

33
00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.600
She'll get here long before they do.

34
00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.680
And Ned Stark always said 500 men
Could hold Winterfell against 10.000.

35
00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.360
-( dogs barking )
-Man: we have a scent!

36
00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.960
The hounds have the scent.

37
00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.360
Come. maester. don't look so grim.

38
00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.960
It's all just a game.

39
00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.480
Osha:
We should have took more food.

40
00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:32.440
We couldn't risk
Going to the kitchens.

41
00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.920
Those people all love you.

42
00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.400
They would have given
You whatever you needed.

43
00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.240
And if Theon found out.
He'd hang them.

44
00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.800
-The boy can't survive on walnuts.
-I'm fine.

45
00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.080
We've been walking
Since before sunrise.

46
00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.400
-Even Hodor will tire.
-Hodor.

47
00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:49.320
-Even you. sweet giant.
-( chuckles ) Hodor.

48
00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.920
( children shouting )

49
00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.080
Wait. I know that farm.

50
00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:57.640
I sent those two
Winterfell orphans there.

51
00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.520
Jack and billy.

52
00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.320
-They'll give us some food.
-We can't risk it.

53
00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.000
If Theon tracks us here.
He'll torture them

54
00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.840
Until he finds out where we are.

55
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.240
Billy climbs a tree
Better than anyone.

56
00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.000
You've never seen me
Climb a tree. little man.

57
00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.800
They'll be after us with hounds.
We got a good start on them.

58
00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:16.040
But we can't outrun hounds forever.

59
00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:43.000
Did you pull a knife
On me in the night?

60
00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.400
What's the matter?

61
00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.160
Can't be the first time
You pressed your bone

62
00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.640
Against a woman's ass.

63
00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.480
Let's move.

64
00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.280
Oh. it is the first time.

65
00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:12.520
How old are you. boy?

66
00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.120
I'm a man of the night's watch.

67
00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:19.480
You're a boy who's
Never been with a girl.

68
00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.880
Don't your stones start to hurt

69
00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:27.280
If your bone never gets...

70
00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.320
Don't call them that.

71
00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.520
What. stones?

72
00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.200
Or bone?

73
00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.520
Neither.

74
00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.640
Both.

75
00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.080
Move!

76
00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.760
Ygritte:
I heard they get all swollen

77
00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:51.040
And bruised if you don't use them.

78
00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:52.800
Of course. maybe that's
Just what the lads say

79
00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:55.240
When they want me
Feeling sorry for them.

80
00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.400
As if I'd feel sorry for them.

81
00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:00.920
Are there no girl crows?

82
00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:04.640
There are no women
Of the night's watch. no.

83
00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.680
So the lads just do it
With each other?

84
00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:08.560
No.

85
00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:10.960
-Never?
-Never.

86
00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:13.440
We swore an oath.

87
00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.600
You have sheep at the wall?

88
00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.760
With your hands. then?

89
00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:22.760
No wonder you're all so miserable.

90
00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:24.240
Would you please shut up?

91
00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.120
( mocking )
Would you please shut up?

92
00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:29.680
You think you're
Better than me. crow.

93
00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.120
-I'm a free woman...
-You're a free woman?

94
00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:34.360
I might be your prisoner.
But I'm a free woman.

95
00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.280
If you're my prisoner.
You're not a free woman.

96
00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:37.760
That's what "prisoner" means.

97
00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:39.680
And you think you're free?

98
00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:42.720
You swore some stupid oath

99
00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:44.240
And now you can never touch a girl.

100
00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.640
It was my choice to say the words.

101
00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:48.400
-So you don't like girls?
-Of course I like girls.

102
00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.200
But you chose
Never to touch them.

103
00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:52.880
That's the price you pay if you want
To be a man of the night's watch.

104
00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.680
So instead of getting
Naked with a girl.

105
00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.200
You'd prefer to invade our lands...

106
00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:57.840
Invade your lands?

107
00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.880
Wildlings raid
Our lands all the time.

108
00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.520
Some of them tried to kill
My little brother. a crippled boy!

109
00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:04.440
They're not your lands!

110
00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:06.520
We've been here the whole time.

111
00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:09.880
You lot came along
And just put up a big wall
And said it was yours.

112
00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:12.360
My father was Ned Stark.

113
00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:14.400
I have the blood of the first men.

114
00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:17.440
My ancestors lived here.
Same as yours.

115
00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.600
So why are you fighting us?

116
00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.160
Go on.

117
00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.600
Now I want you
To tell me what happened.

118
00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:49.480
-Guard: come on. this way.
-( man screaming )

119
00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:53.000
Come on. speak up. Speak up.

120
00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:58.080
( sniffs )

121
00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.640
Wolfsbane...

122
00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:03.120
A rare substance.

123
00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:05.480
This is no common assassin.

124
00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.680
We hanged 20 men last night.

125
00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:10.280
I don't care if you hanged 100.

126
00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.800
A man tried to kill me.

127
00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.720
I want his name and I want his head.

128
00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.200
Mountain:
We think it was an infiltrator

129
00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:18.000
From the brotherhood without banners.

130
00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:20.640
Pretentious name
For a band of outlaws.

131
00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.200
We can't allow rebels
Behind our lines

132
00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:25.200
To harass us with impunity.

133
00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:27.240
We look like fools
And they look like heroes.

134
00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.920
That's how kings fall.

135
00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.040
I want them dead. every one.

136
00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:32.760
Killing them isn't the problem.

137
00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.640
It's finding them.

138
00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.880
Have you gone soft. Clegane?

139
00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:38.880
I always thought you had
A talent for violence.

140
00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:42.360
Burn the villages. burn the farms.

141
00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.680
Let them know what it means
To choose the wrong side.

142
00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:46.160
Mmm.

143
00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:50.560
Is that mutton?

144
00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.040
Yes. my lord.

145
00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:53.520
Don't like mutton.

146
00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:56.400
I'll bring something else.

147
00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:58.480
Leave it.

148
00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.880
-Are you hungry?
-No.

149
00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:04.920
Of course you are. Eat.

150
00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:08.120
I'll... Eat in the kitchen later.

151
00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:12.120
It's bad manners
To refuse a lord's offer.

152
00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:14.240
Sit.

153
00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:17.120
Eat.

154
00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.480
You're small for your age.

155
00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.520
I suppose you've been
Underfed your whole life.

156
00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:26.400
I eat a lot.

157
00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.200
-I just don't grow.
-Hmm.

158
00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:36.160
This will be my last war.

159
00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.160
Win or lose.

160
00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.280
Have you ever lost before?

161
00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:44.080
Do you think I'd be in my position
If I had lost a war?

162
00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:54.480
But this is the one
I'll be remembered for.

163
00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.840
The "war of five kings"
They're calling it.

164
00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:01.320
My legacy will be determined
In the coming months.

165
00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:05.520
Do you know what legacy means?

166
00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:10.040
It's what you pass down
To your children

167
00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:13.240
And your children's children.

168
00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.120
It's what remains of you
When you're gone.

169
00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:22.720
Harren the black thought this castle
Would be his legacy.

170
00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:27.040
The greatest fortress ever built...

171
00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:30.440
The tallest towers.
The strongest walls.

172
00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:33.840
The great hall had 35 hearths.

173
00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:36.920
35. Can you imagine?

174
00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:38.400
Look at it now...

175
00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:41.240
A blasted ruin.

176
00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:44.280
Do you know what happened?

177
00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:46.600
Dragons?

178
00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:50.480
Yes. dragons happened.

179
00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:57.040
Harrenhal was built to withstand
An attack from the land.

180
00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:02.320
A million men
Could have marched on these walls

181
00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:04.600
And a million men
Would have been repelled.

182
00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:10.000
But an attack from the air
With dragon fire... mm.

183
00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:13.240
Harren and all his sons
Roasted alive within these walls.

184
00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:18.040
Aegon Targaryen changed the rules.

185
00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:20.880
That's why every child alive
Still knows his name

186
00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.920
300 years after his death.

187
00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:25.200
Aegon and his sisters.

188
00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:27.760
Mm?

189
00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:30.920
It wasn't just Aegon
Riding his dragon.

190
00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:32.680
It was Rhaenys and Visenya. too.

191
00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:34.960
Correct.

192
00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:37.040
A student of history. are you?

193
00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.480
Rhaenys rode Meraxes.

194
00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:41.200
Visenya rode Vhagar.

195
00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:45.360
I'm sure I knew that
When I was a boy.

196
00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:49.520
Visenya Targaryen
Was a great warrior.

197
00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:52.360
She had a Valyrian steel sword
She called “Dark Sister.”

198
00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:54.640
Hmm.

199
00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:56.640
She's a heroine of yours. I take it?

200
00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.560
Aren't most girls more interested

201
00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:01.520
In the pretty maidens
From the songs?

202
00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:03.400
Jonquil with the flowers
In her hair?

203
00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:05.800
-Most girls are idiots.
-Ha!

204
00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:09.480
You remind me of my daughter.

205
00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.120
Where did you learn all this stuff

206
00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:15.840
About Visenya and her
Valyrian steel sword?

207
00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.640
From my father.

208
00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:24.160
He was a well-read stonemason.

209
00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:28.160
Can't say I've ever met
A literate stonemason.

210
00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:30.720
Have you met many
Stonemasons. my lord?

211
00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.080
Careful now. girl.

212
00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:37.240
I enjoy you. but be careful.

213
00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:39.960
Take that back to the kitchen.

214
00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:41.680
Eat what you want.

215
00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:46.520
And. girl.

216
00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:50.040
M'lord.

217
00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:54.160
Lowborn girls say "m'lord."

218
00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:56.400
Not "my lord."

219
00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:58.600
If you're going
To pose as a commoner.

220
00:13:58.760 --> 00:14:00.600
You should do it properly.

221
00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:03.680
My mother served Lady Dustin

222
00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:06.520
For many years. my lord.

223
00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:09.720
She taught me how to speak
Proper... properly.

224
00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:13.640
You're too smart for your own good.

225
00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:16.400
-Has anyone told you that?
-Yes.

226
00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:18.960
Go on.

227
00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:33.160
I beg pardon. ser.

228
00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:35.400
I should have come to you after

229
00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.640
To thank you for saving me.

230
00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:39.720
-You were so brave.
-Brave?

231
00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:43.200
A dog doesn't need courage
To chase off rats.

232
00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.880
Does it give you joy to scare people?

233
00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:48.760
No. It gives me joy to kill people.

234
00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:51.480
Spare me. You can't tell me

235
00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:53.920
Lord Eddard Stark of Winterfell
Never killed a man.

236
00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:56.880
It was his duty. He never liked it.

237
00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.000
Is that what he told you?

238
00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:01.280
He lied.

239
00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:04.240
Killing is the sweetest
Thing there is.

240
00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:06.680
Why are you always
So hateful?

241
00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.480
You'll be glad
Of the hateful things I do

242
00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:11.160
Someday when you're queen
And I'm all that stands

243
00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:13.360
Between you and your beloved king.

244
00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:24.320
I've demanded a meeting
Of the thirteen.

245
00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:26.080
One of them did this
Or knows who did.

246
00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:27.600
You are one of the thirteen.

247
00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.720
If I wanted your dragons.
I would have taken them.

248
00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:32.840
-They mean nothing
To me on their own.
-Nothing?

249
00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.320
They're more valuable
Than anything in the world.

250
00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:37.920
Shall we look inside my vault
And see what selling your dragons

251
00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.800
Would buy me I cannot buy already?

252
00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.880
We will get them back.

253
00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.640
There is no we.

254
00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:46.280
So why would you help me
Get them back?

255
00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:47.920
I took you under my protection

256
00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:49.880
In front of the rulers of my city.

257
00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:52.800
A man is what others
Say he is and no more.

258
00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:55.360
If they say that
Xaro Xhoan Daxos is a liar.

259
00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:57.720
My word is worth nothing.

260
00:15:57.880 --> 00:16:00.360
I cannot let this thing
Happen to you under my roof.

261
00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:02.520
But it did happen under your roof.

262
00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:06.040
Khaleesi. many times
In my life I have been...

263
00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:07.560
I don't care where you've been.

264
00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:33.600
You think we're savages
Because we don't live
In stone castles.

265
00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:37.240
We can't make steel
As good as yours. it's true. but...

266
00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:39.680
We're free.

267
00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:42.880
If someone tried to tell us
We couldn't lie down
As man and woman.

268
00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:45.400
We'd shove a spear up his ass.

269
00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:47.240
We don't go serving some shit king

270
00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.760
Who's only king
Because his father was.

271
00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:53.480
No. No. you serve Mance Rayder.
The king-beyond-the-wall.

272
00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:56.280
We chose Mance Rayder to lead us.

273
00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:58.640
He was a crow. same as you.

274
00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:00.640
But he wanted to be free.

275
00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:05.120
You could be free. too.

276
00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:06.720
You don't need to live
Your whole life

277
00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.880
Taking commands from old men.

278
00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:11.880
Wake up when you want to wake up.

279
00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:14.800
I could show you the streams to fish.
The woods to hunt.

280
00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:18.560
Build yourself a cabin and find
A woman to lie with in the night.

281
00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:22.120
You're a pretty lad.

282
00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:25.160
The girls would claw
Each other's eyes out
To get naked with you.

283
00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:30.080
Walk.

284
00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:33.400
I could teach you how to do it.

285
00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:35.520
I know how to do it.

286
00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:41.000
You know nothing. Jon Snow.

287
00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:03.000
( chatter )

288
00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:10.360
And what did she say?

289
00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.920
She admired your spirit. your grace.

290
00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:14.720
And what then?

291
00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:18.960
She. uh...

292
00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:20.880
If every man were held accountable

293
00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:22.760
For the actions
Of every distant relative.

294
00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:25.720
Ser Alton. we'd all hang.

295
00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:31.880
She tore the paper
In half. your grace.

296
00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:33.360
You've acted with honor.

297
00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:35.320
I thank you for it.

298
00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:38.320
Lord Karstark. see that
Ser Alton's pen is clean.

299
00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:39.800
And give him a hot supper.

300
00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:42.240
Ser Alton's pen
Is occupied. your grace.

301
00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:44.560
The prisoners from the yellow fork.

302
00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:46.640
Too many prisoners.

303
00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:49.320
Is there room for Ser Alton?

304
00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:52.320
Does he need to lie down?

305
00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:56.440
Have the men build him a new pen.

306
00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:59.080
Put him in with
The Kingslayer for now.

307
00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:01.120
Have your boy watch over them.

308
00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:03.680
Torrhen.

309
00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:05.280
That will be all.

310
00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:13.120
Your grace.

311
00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:15.160
A minute of your time?

312
00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:31.120
I've been treating your wounded men.

313
00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:35.200
And my enemies
As some of my bannermen
Are fond of mentioning.

314
00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:36.800
They're not my enemies.

315
00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:39.000
That's what I tell my bannermen.

316
00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:41.480
I've already run through
The supplies I brought with me.

317
00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:42.960
Some are easily replaced...

318
00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:45.760
Egg yolks. turpentine. oil of roses.

319
00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:48.080
But some are not.

320
00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:50.920
I need silk for stitching.

321
00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:55.240
I need fennel root
For those with fever. willow bark.

322
00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:57.320
Mostly I need milk of the poppy.

323
00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:00.400
You saw what it was like
To amputate a foot without any.

324
00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:03.960
I assume there will be more loss
Of limb before this war is over.

325
00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:07.640
-If you need help finding these...
-I know where to find them.

326
00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:11.440
I'm sorry. I shouldn't interrupt you.

327
00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:14.720
Continue. my lady.

328
00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:21.600
-You're riding to the crag
To negotiate a surrender?
-Yes.

329
00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:24.680
The crag will have a maester
And he will have what I need.

330
00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:26.800
I expect he will.

331
00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:28.800
If I could write a list...

332
00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:30.920
Come with me to the crag.

333
00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:34.000
I don't think that will be...

334
00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:36.280
Let the maester show you his stores.

335
00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:40.320
I want the wounded men
To be treated well...

336
00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:42.120
All the wounded men.

337
00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:47.480
( dog barking )

338
00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.880
Woman:
Children. come inside. quick.

339
00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.200
Hurry up!

340
00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:56.960
-( dog barking )
-Man: can't find anything. ser.

341
00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:59.760
-They've lost the scent.
-Try again.

342
00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:01.320
We've circled this farmhouse twice.

343
00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:02.920
There's no sign of them.

344
00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:06.720
We could start the search fresh
In the morning. my lord.

345
00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:08.640
I'm looking at spending
The rest of my life

346
00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:11.440
Being treated like a fool
And a eunuch by my own people.

347
00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:13.320
Ask yourself.
"is there anything I wouldn't do

348
00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:14.800
To stop that from happening?"

349
00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:17.000
The hounds will find the scent again.

350
00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:19.160
I'll beat them until they do.

351
00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:22.800
I'll whip every man here
Until I have both those boys in hand.

352
00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:25.720
And once I've got them.
The pampered little shits...

353
00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:29.520
It's better to be cruel than weak.

354
00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.720
Prince Theon.

355
00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:33.720
-Where are they?
-Who. m'lord?

356
00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:37.080
-The Stark boys. Where are they?
-I don't know. I seen no one.

357
00:21:37.240 --> 00:21:40.360
-Oh!
-Think harder.

358
00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:44.400
I swear. m'lord. I don't know.

359
00:21:44.560 --> 00:21:47.160
My lord. over here.

360
00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:52.360
I think I've found
What we're looking for.

361
00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:03.920
Send the old man home.

362
00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:10.600
Go back to Winterfell.

363
00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:12.240
Take him back.

364
00:22:14.760 --> 00:22:16.880
Theon. don't do this.

365
00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:22.640
( birds chirping )

366
00:22:34.760 --> 00:22:36.320
You came back.

367
00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:38.400
As soon as I heard.

368
00:22:38.560 --> 00:22:40.920
Do you know anything?

369
00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:43.640
-Irri is dead.
-I know.

370
00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:46.920
-She was a good...
-She's dead.

371
00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:48.720
She died alone.

372
00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:50.880
She died for me
And I couldn't protect her.

373
00:22:52.280 --> 00:22:53.640
Doreah?

374
00:22:53.800 --> 00:22:55.520
We can't find her.

375
00:22:57.040 --> 00:22:59.760
She must be dead. too.

376
00:22:59.920 --> 00:23:03.240
I led my people out of the red waste
And into the slaughterhouse.

377
00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:05.120
I should have been here.

378
00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:08.560
You went to find me a ship.

379
00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:10.640
My place is by your side.

380
00:23:10.800 --> 00:23:12.920
I shouldn't have left you
Alone with these people.

381
00:23:13.080 --> 00:23:14.600
These people?

382
00:23:14.760 --> 00:23:16.880
They are not to be trusted.

383
00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:19.520
And who is to be trusted?

384
00:23:19.680 --> 00:23:21.000
Who are my people?

385
00:23:21.160 --> 00:23:23.280
The Targaryens?

386
00:23:23.440 --> 00:23:25.040
I only knew one... my brother.

387
00:23:25.200 --> 00:23:27.240
And he would have let
1.000 men rape me

388
00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:29.200
If it had got him the crown.

389
00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:30.840
The Dothraki?

390
00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:34.320
Most of them turned on me the day
That Khal Drogo fell from his horse.

391
00:23:34.480 --> 00:23:35.960
Your people are in Westeros.

392
00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:38.560
The people in Westeros
Don't know I'm alive.

393
00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:40.560
-They will soon enough.
-And then what?

394
00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:42.840
They'll pray for my return?

395
00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:45.160
They'll wave dragon banners
And shout my name?

396
00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:48.240
That's what my brother believed
And he was a fool.

397
00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:50.560
You are not your brother.

398
00:23:50.720 --> 00:23:53.040
Trust me. khaleesi.

399
00:23:53.200 --> 00:23:55.120
There it is...

400
00:23:55.280 --> 00:23:57.360
"trust me."

401
00:23:57.520 --> 00:23:59.840
And it's you I should trust.
Ser Jorah?

402
00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.680
Only you?

403
00:24:04.400 --> 00:24:07.600
I don't need trust any longer.

404
00:24:07.760 --> 00:24:10.480
I don't want it
And I don't have room for it.

405
00:24:10.640 --> 00:24:12.400
You are too young to be so...

406
00:24:12.560 --> 00:24:14.400
And you are too familiar.

407
00:24:18.920 --> 00:24:21.200
Forgive me. khaleesi.

408
00:24:22.800 --> 00:24:25.760
No one can survive
In this world without help.

409
00:24:25.920 --> 00:24:29.600
No one. Let me help you. please.

410
00:24:29.760 --> 00:24:32.320
Tell me how.

411
00:24:33.800 --> 00:24:35.320
Find my dragons.

412
00:24:43.080 --> 00:24:45.560
Ygritte:
How long till we get
Back to your crows?

413
00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:48.680
We're close.

414
00:24:48.840 --> 00:24:51.960
What. a day? A half-day?

415
00:24:55.840 --> 00:24:58.400
You don't know. do you?

416
00:24:58.560 --> 00:25:01.080
-Do you even know where they are?
-We're close.

417
00:25:02.960 --> 00:25:05.080
What do you think they'll say
When they hear about you and me?

418
00:25:05.240 --> 00:25:07.000
Nothing happened between you and me.

419
00:25:07.160 --> 00:25:10.320
"I swear it.
Old master king crow. ser.

420
00:25:10.480 --> 00:25:12.920
We were only close
Together for warmth.

421
00:25:13.080 --> 00:25:14.520
And then I felt it.

422
00:25:14.680 --> 00:25:17.200
Right up against
Me backside like a club.

423
00:25:17.360 --> 00:25:19.520
I can show you the bruise
On me tailbone.

424
00:25:19.680 --> 00:25:23.000
And before I knew
What was where. his... his...

425
00:25:23.160 --> 00:25:25.880
Well. it was all out in the open.
All angry as you like.

426
00:25:26.040 --> 00:25:29.720
And I didn't want to want it.
But. oh. I did!

427
00:25:29.880 --> 00:25:32.520
And he spread me legs and... ruined.

428
00:25:32.680 --> 00:25:34.200
The shame of it.

429
00:25:34.360 --> 00:25:36.360
Now I can never marry
A perfumed lord.

430
00:25:36.520 --> 00:25:39.880
-What will me poor
Savage father say?"
-Turn back around.

431
00:25:40.040 --> 00:25:41.840
"and I thought
That we were done. but he said.

432
00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:44.520
( deep voice )
'Turn back around.'"

433
00:25:44.680 --> 00:25:47.160
( normal voice )
I'll tell you what. Jon Snow.

434
00:25:47.320 --> 00:25:49.200
Since it's going to be
Your word against mine.

435
00:25:49.360 --> 00:25:52.880
And since you can't talk
About it without blushing.

436
00:25:53.040 --> 00:25:55.720
We may as well just.

437
00:25:56.720 --> 00:25:58.800
What. right here in the muck?

438
00:25:58.960 --> 00:26:00.800
I'll keep you warm enough.

439
00:26:02.880 --> 00:26:06.320
-Are you that afraid of it?
-That's enough.

440
00:26:06.480 --> 00:26:08.720
Oh. it's nice

441
00:26:08.880 --> 00:26:11.600
And wet and warm.

442
00:26:11.760 --> 00:26:13.240
Enough!

443
00:26:14.560 --> 00:26:16.040
It don't have teeth.

444
00:26:23.920 --> 00:26:25.800
All right!

445
00:26:25.960 --> 00:26:27.360
All right.

446
00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:30.320
Gods. you're dull.

447
00:26:32.040 --> 00:26:34.280
( grunting )

448
00:26:40.440 --> 00:26:41.920
( sword rings )

449
00:26:52.680 --> 00:26:54.320
( Ygritte whistles )

450
00:27:05.320 --> 00:27:07.400
Should have took me
While you had the chance.

451
00:27:15.240 --> 00:27:17.640
( Sansa crying )

452
00:27:17.800 --> 00:27:19.480
( Sansa crying )
No. no!

453
00:27:26.920 --> 00:27:28.440
-( screams )
-( laughs )

454
00:27:28.600 --> 00:27:30.400
( screams )

455
00:27:38.240 --> 00:27:41.120
No. Oh. no.

456
00:27:50.800 --> 00:27:53.280
( whimpering )

457
00:27:56.440 --> 00:27:58.800
It's all right. Give me that.

458
00:27:58.960 --> 00:28:02.720
If the queen sees
I can have Joffrey's children now...

459
00:28:02.880 --> 00:28:04.280
Help me flip it over.

460
00:28:20.600 --> 00:28:23.120
-Where are you going?
-To tell her grace.

461
00:28:25.080 --> 00:28:27.040
You'll say nothing to anyone.

462
00:28:27.200 --> 00:28:29.040
Do you understand?

463
00:28:48.600 --> 00:28:51.720
Your mother might have prepared you.

464
00:28:51.880 --> 00:28:54.080
You flowered. my dear. No more.

465
00:28:54.240 --> 00:28:57.000
My mother told me.
But I thought it would be different.

466
00:28:57.160 --> 00:29:01.520
-In what way?
-I thought it would be less...

467
00:29:01.680 --> 00:29:04.600
Less messy.

468
00:29:04.760 --> 00:29:07.200
Wait until you bear the child.

469
00:29:08.920 --> 00:29:10.280
You're a woman now.

470
00:29:10.440 --> 00:29:13.120
Do you have any idea
What that means?

471
00:29:13.280 --> 00:29:15.600
I'm fit to bear children
For the king?

472
00:29:15.760 --> 00:29:17.920
A prospect that once delighted you...

473
00:29:18.080 --> 00:29:20.360
Bringing little princes
And princesses into the world.

474
00:29:20.520 --> 00:29:23.800
The greatest honor for a queen.

475
00:29:28.200 --> 00:29:31.080
Joffrey has always been difficult.

476
00:29:31.240 --> 00:29:33.080
Even his birth.
I labored a day and a half

477
00:29:33.240 --> 00:29:35.160
To bring him into this world.

478
00:29:35.320 --> 00:29:37.520
You cannot imagine the pain.

479
00:29:37.680 --> 00:29:40.760
I screamed so loudly. I was sure
Robert would hear me in the kingswood.

480
00:29:40.920 --> 00:29:43.680
His grace was not with you?

481
00:29:43.840 --> 00:29:45.200
Robert was hunting.

482
00:29:45.360 --> 00:29:46.840
That was his custom.

483
00:29:49.640 --> 00:29:52.120
Whenever my time was near.

484
00:29:52.280 --> 00:29:54.600
My royal husband
Would flee to the trees

485
00:29:54.760 --> 00:29:59.240
With his huntsmen and his hounds.

486
00:29:59.400 --> 00:30:00.840
And when he returned.
He would present me

487
00:30:01.000 --> 00:30:03.920
With some pelts or a stag's head.

488
00:30:04.080 --> 00:30:05.600
And I would present him with a baby.

489
00:30:07.640 --> 00:30:10.000
Not that I wanted
Him there. mind you.

490
00:30:10.160 --> 00:30:12.960
I had Grand Maester Pycelle.
an army of midwives.

491
00:30:13.120 --> 00:30:15.000
And I had my brother.

492
00:30:15.160 --> 00:30:18.080
When they told Jaime
He wasn't allowed in
The birthing room.

493
00:30:18.240 --> 00:30:21.320
He smiled and asked
Which one of them

494
00:30:21.480 --> 00:30:23.320
Proposed to keep him out.

495
00:30:26.480 --> 00:30:28.720
Joffrey will show you
No such devotion.

496
00:30:31.200 --> 00:30:33.640
You may never love the king.

497
00:30:33.800 --> 00:30:35.360
But you will love his children.

498
00:30:35.520 --> 00:30:38.760
I love his grace with all my heart.

499
00:30:38.920 --> 00:30:41.320
That's so very touching to hear.

500
00:30:45.800 --> 00:30:47.960
Permit me to share
Some womanly wisdom with you

501
00:30:48.120 --> 00:30:50.840
On this very special day.

502
00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:54.640
The more people you love.
The weaker you are.

503
00:30:54.800 --> 00:30:58.040
You'll do things for them
That you know you shouldn't do.

504
00:30:58.200 --> 00:31:01.440
You'll act the fool
To make them happy.
To keep them safe.

505
00:31:04.080 --> 00:31:06.600
Love no one but your children.

506
00:31:06.760 --> 00:31:10.000
On that front.
A mother has no choice.

507
00:31:10.160 --> 00:31:14.400
But... Shouldn't
I love Joffrey. your grace?

508
00:31:16.960 --> 00:31:19.480
You can try.

509
00:31:19.640 --> 00:31:21.280
Little dove.

510
00:31:27.120 --> 00:31:29.040
( chatter )

511
00:31:36.720 --> 00:31:39.200
Who did you say
Your mother was again?

512
00:31:39.360 --> 00:31:40.920
Cinda Lannister.

513
00:31:41.080 --> 00:31:42.600
Is she the fat one?

514
00:31:43.960 --> 00:31:45.440
Well. perhaps she's gotten
A little larger than she...

515
00:31:45.600 --> 00:31:49.040
No. no.
There's only one fat Lannister.

516
00:31:49.200 --> 00:31:51.680
If she was your mother.
You'd know it.

517
00:31:53.440 --> 00:31:56.280
I... I squired
For you once. you know?

518
00:31:57.520 --> 00:31:58.880
When?

519
00:31:59.040 --> 00:32:02.240
The tournament the day
Of Willem Frey's wedding.

520
00:32:02.400 --> 00:32:05.120
I went to Willem Frey's wedding?

521
00:32:05.280 --> 00:32:06.800
You did.

522
00:32:06.960 --> 00:32:09.240
Your squire had gotten
So drunk the night before that he...

523
00:32:09.400 --> 00:32:11.320
He threw up on his horse

524
00:32:11.480 --> 00:32:12.920
On the way to the tourney grounds.

525
00:32:13.080 --> 00:32:15.280
-What was his name?
-Bryan.

526
00:32:15.440 --> 00:32:18.520
( laughs )
Poor lad.

527
00:32:18.680 --> 00:32:21.240
That was my brother's doing.
I seem to recall.

528
00:32:23.400 --> 00:32:25.560
I remember you.

529
00:32:25.720 --> 00:32:28.280
You had never squired
For anyone before.

530
00:32:28.440 --> 00:32:30.080
That's right.
I ran up and volunteered.

531
00:32:30.240 --> 00:32:33.360
"let me. my lord. Let me."

532
00:32:33.520 --> 00:32:35.800
My father was furious.

533
00:32:35.960 --> 00:32:37.520
Afraid I'd embarrass our family

534
00:32:37.680 --> 00:32:39.760
In front of the family.

535
00:32:41.880 --> 00:32:43.360
You didn't. though.

536
00:32:43.520 --> 00:32:45.840
-You really remember?
-Mm.

537
00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:48.040
You knew when you were needed
And when to go away.

538
00:32:48.200 --> 00:32:49.680
It's a rare talent.

539
00:32:49.840 --> 00:32:53.200
Most of my squires. they mean well.

540
00:32:53.360 --> 00:32:56.560
But young men with big jobs.
They tend to overdo them.

541
00:32:56.720 --> 00:32:58.440
Well. when I think
Back to that day...

542
00:32:58.600 --> 00:33:00.080
( hisses )

543
00:33:07.920 --> 00:33:09.720
You were saying?

544
00:33:09.880 --> 00:33:12.160
I...

545
00:33:12.320 --> 00:33:14.920
Never mind. It's embarrassing.

546
00:33:15.080 --> 00:33:17.480
More embarrassing
Than being chained to a post

547
00:33:17.640 --> 00:33:19.160
Covered in your own shit?

548
00:33:20.680 --> 00:33:23.080
I remember everything
About that day...

549
00:33:23.240 --> 00:33:25.400
Your helmet. your horse.

550
00:33:25.560 --> 00:33:28.000
The rake lines in the dirt
along the list.

551
00:33:28.160 --> 00:33:31.600
Where the sun was in the sky
when you knocked
Balon Swann from his horse.

552
00:33:31.760 --> 00:33:34.600
And the dent in your shield
When you handed it back to me.

553
00:33:36.720 --> 00:33:39.400
I'll remember it all until I die.

554
00:33:41.080 --> 00:33:42.760
That was the best day of my life.

555
00:33:45.720 --> 00:33:49.520
And I remember being on the field
After it was over.

556
00:33:49.680 --> 00:33:52.840
All the competitors were done.
I was the last one out there.

557
00:33:54.920 --> 00:33:57.560
And I couldn't leave.

558
00:33:57.720 --> 00:33:59.680
I couldn't bring myself
To go and sit with my family

559
00:33:59.840 --> 00:34:01.800
At a table so far
On the edge of the feast

560
00:34:01.960 --> 00:34:04.040
You could barely even see the bride.

561
00:34:04.200 --> 00:34:07.240
And I couldn't bear to tell them what
It had been like squiring for you

562
00:34:07.400 --> 00:34:10.840
When I knew that they could
Never have the faintest idea
What I was talking about.

563
00:34:12.040 --> 00:34:13.880
I understand completely.

564
00:34:14.040 --> 00:34:16.840
How could you?

565
00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:19.760
S-sorry. I... I didn't
Mean to doubt you.

566
00:34:19.920 --> 00:34:23.200
-It's just that I...
-I was 16 once.

567
00:34:23.360 --> 00:34:26.400
I also had to replace
Someone's squire on short notice.

568
00:34:26.560 --> 00:34:28.080
Which knight was it?

569
00:34:28.240 --> 00:34:30.720
Barristan selmy.

570
00:34:32.200 --> 00:34:33.880
The fight against
The kingswood outlaws.

571
00:34:34.040 --> 00:34:36.400
Before your time.

572
00:34:36.560 --> 00:34:37.880
What was he like?

573
00:34:38.040 --> 00:34:40.560
( sighs )

574
00:34:40.720 --> 00:34:43.880
He was

575
00:34:44.040 --> 00:34:46.720
A painter.

576
00:34:46.880 --> 00:34:49.800
A painter who only used red.

577
00:34:52.360 --> 00:34:56.160
I couldn't imagine being
Able to fight like that.

578
00:34:56.320 --> 00:34:58.440
Not back then.

579
00:34:58.600 --> 00:35:03.120
And to help him do that.
To be a part of something
That perfect...

580
00:35:04.800 --> 00:35:07.080
I don't need to explain
How that felt. not to you.

581
00:35:08.160 --> 00:35:09.680
It's hard to put into words.

582
00:35:09.840 --> 00:35:12.840
It's like stepping into a dream

583
00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:15.880
You've been dreaming
For as long as you can remember

584
00:35:16.040 --> 00:35:17.760
And finding out that the dream

585
00:35:17.920 --> 00:35:20.520
Is more real than your life.

586
00:35:23.000 --> 00:35:25.840
Leaving that battlefield was

587
00:35:26.000 --> 00:35:28.000
Like being dragged off to prison.

588
00:35:28.160 --> 00:35:31.120
-Did you squire for him again?
-No.

589
00:35:32.320 --> 00:35:34.840
I didn't have your gift.

590
00:35:35.000 --> 00:35:38.160
He couldn't take a step
Without stepping on me.

591
00:35:38.320 --> 00:35:41.280
I was awful. a complete liability...

592
00:35:41.440 --> 00:35:44.840
Until one of the outlaws

593
00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:48.120
Decided to take on
A 16-year-old squire.

594
00:35:53.720 --> 00:35:56.280
It's a good thing I am who I am.

595
00:35:56.440 --> 00:35:59.600
( chuckles )
I'd have been useless
At anything else.

596
00:36:04.120 --> 00:36:06.960
I'm not well-suited
For imprisonment.

597
00:36:07.120 --> 00:36:08.680
Shocking. I know.

598
00:36:08.840 --> 00:36:10.400
Some men are.

599
00:36:10.560 --> 00:36:13.760
Ned Stark... I imagine he made

600
00:36:13.920 --> 00:36:17.120
An excellent prisoner
Right up until the end.

601
00:36:17.280 --> 00:36:20.440
But me. though... my life has left me

602
00:36:20.600 --> 00:36:23.240
Uniquely unfit for constraint.

603
00:36:25.000 --> 00:36:26.400
Have you thought about...?

604
00:36:26.560 --> 00:36:28.000
Of course.

605
00:36:28.160 --> 00:36:30.640
-Every day.
-And?

606
00:36:32.440 --> 00:36:36.720
Good prisoners breed
Good jailers. apparently.

607
00:36:36.880 --> 00:36:38.640
The starks are very careful.

608
00:36:39.960 --> 00:36:43.840
But there is a way. I think.

609
00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:46.440
It wasn't possible until now.

610
00:36:46.600 --> 00:36:49.440
What is it?

611
00:36:53.600 --> 00:36:56.400
-It's actually quite simple.
-Well. let me help you.

612
00:36:56.560 --> 00:36:59.040
You'll only have to do one thing.

613
00:36:59.200 --> 00:37:00.720
Tell me.

614
00:37:03.400 --> 00:37:05.320
You'll have to die.

615
00:37:16.280 --> 00:37:18.200
( crunching )

616
00:37:34.800 --> 00:37:37.120
( choking )

617
00:37:40.680 --> 00:37:43.000
( bone breaks )

618
00:37:48.520 --> 00:37:51.080
( bird screeching )

619
00:37:56.640 --> 00:37:58.840
Jorah the andal.

620
00:37:59.000 --> 00:38:02.040
This man must sail past old Valyria.

621
00:38:02.200 --> 00:38:06.160
All who travel too close to the doom
Must have protection.

622
00:38:06.320 --> 00:38:08.000
I didn't come here for lessons.

623
00:38:08.160 --> 00:38:10.080
No. you came for the dragons.

624
00:38:10.240 --> 00:38:12.000
You have them?

625
00:38:13.320 --> 00:38:15.160
Where are they?

626
00:38:15.320 --> 00:38:17.240
Draw your sword.

627
00:38:17.400 --> 00:38:20.560
See what your steel is worth.

628
00:38:23.280 --> 00:38:26.880
You want to please
The mother of dragons.

629
00:38:31.720 --> 00:38:34.000
You love her.

630
00:38:36.960 --> 00:38:38.880
Where are the dragons?

631
00:38:40.480 --> 00:38:42.640
Will you betray her again.
Jorah the Andal?

632
00:38:47.240 --> 00:38:49.720
Will you betray her again?

633
00:38:52.000 --> 00:38:53.440
Never.

634
00:38:59.200 --> 00:39:01.280
The thief you seek

635
00:39:01.440 --> 00:39:04.120
Is with her now.

636
00:39:08.640 --> 00:39:10.720
Spice king:
I did not leave
The comfort of my home

637
00:39:10.880 --> 00:39:12.480
To come to yours
And be called a thief.

638
00:39:12.640 --> 00:39:14.280
No one is calling you a thief.

639
00:39:14.440 --> 00:39:16.000
Who is she to accuse us?

640
00:39:16.160 --> 00:39:17.960
Please. they're my children.

641
00:39:18.120 --> 00:39:20.120
-I'm begging you.
-Begging us?

642
00:39:20.280 --> 00:39:22.560
It wasn't very long ago
You were threatening us.

643
00:39:22.720 --> 00:39:25.160
Without me. the dragons will die.

644
00:39:25.320 --> 00:39:27.240
It will be for the best.

645
00:39:27.400 --> 00:39:29.400
Your dragons will bring the world

646
00:39:29.560 --> 00:39:32.080
Nothing but death
And misery. my dear.

647
00:39:32.240 --> 00:39:34.400
If I knew where they were.
I would not tell you.

648
00:39:34.560 --> 00:39:36.320
Pyat Pree:
You are cruel. my friend.

649
00:39:36.480 --> 00:39:39.280
The mother of dragons
Is in the right.

650
00:39:39.440 --> 00:39:42.320
She must be reunited
With her babies.

651
00:39:42.480 --> 00:39:46.000
-I will help you. khaleesi.
-How?

652
00:39:46.160 --> 00:39:49.440
I will take you
To the house of the undying

653
00:39:49.600 --> 00:39:51.320
Where I have put them.

654
00:39:52.640 --> 00:39:54.440
You have my dragons?

655
00:39:54.600 --> 00:39:56.560
When I learned you were
Coming to our city.

656
00:39:56.720 --> 00:39:59.240
I made an arrangement
With the king of Qarth.

657
00:39:59.400 --> 00:40:01.160
( laughter )

658
00:40:01.320 --> 00:40:02.680
He procured them for me.

659
00:40:02.840 --> 00:40:05.480
-But there is no king of Qarth.
-Xaro: there is now.

660
00:40:05.640 --> 00:40:07.440
That was the other half
Of the arrangement.

661
00:40:09.920 --> 00:40:12.680
You would keep your gates
And your minds closed

662
00:40:12.840 --> 00:40:15.720
To everything outside your walls.

663
00:40:15.880 --> 00:40:18.720
But Qarth cannot remain
The greatest city that ever was

664
00:40:18.880 --> 00:40:20.360
If it refuses to change.

665
00:40:20.520 --> 00:40:22.920
I will open Qarth to the world

666
00:40:23.080 --> 00:40:27.040
As I have forced it
To open itself to me.

667
00:40:27.200 --> 00:40:29.920
Your ambition is an inspiration.

668
00:40:30.080 --> 00:40:32.760
But like all upstarts.
You overreach.

669
00:40:32.920 --> 00:40:35.480
Three dragons the size of cats

670
00:40:35.640 --> 00:40:37.640
And an alliance with a charlatan

671
00:40:37.800 --> 00:40:40.120
Do not make you a king.

672
00:40:40.280 --> 00:40:42.240
An upstart and a charlatan?

673
00:40:42.400 --> 00:40:45.160
Empires have been built by less.

674
00:40:45.320 --> 00:40:48.480
Those on the margins
Often come to control the center.

675
00:40:48.640 --> 00:40:50.800
And those in the center
Make room for them.

676
00:40:50.960 --> 00:40:52.320
Willingly or otherwise.

677
00:40:56.720 --> 00:40:59.720
The mother of dragons
Will be with her babies.

678
00:41:01.400 --> 00:41:02.760
She will give them her love

679
00:41:02.920 --> 00:41:05.440
And they will thrive by her side...

680
00:41:08.080 --> 00:41:09.960
Forever.

681
00:41:28.720 --> 00:41:30.960
A mother should be
With her children.

682
00:41:34.080 --> 00:41:36.520
Where will you run to.
Daenerys Stormborn?

683
00:41:36.680 --> 00:41:39.800
Your dragons wait for you
In the house of the undying.

684
00:41:39.960 --> 00:41:41.880
Come see them.

685
00:41:50.760 --> 00:41:52.800
-Lady Stark!
-No farther.

686
00:41:52.960 --> 00:41:54.520
Keep your hands off me. woman.

687
00:41:54.680 --> 00:41:57.840
Don't enter without
An invitation. man.

688
00:41:59.360 --> 00:42:01.480
Forgive me. Lady Stark.

689
00:42:01.640 --> 00:42:03.760
-Catelyn: what is it?
-They caught the Kingslayer.

690
00:42:07.040 --> 00:42:09.560
( men shouting )

691
00:42:09.720 --> 00:42:12.120
-Kill the fucking Kingslayer!
-Hang him!

692
00:42:12.280 --> 00:42:15.600
( men shouting )

693
00:42:15.760 --> 00:42:17.480
You'll die today.

694
00:42:17.640 --> 00:42:19.760
Justice for the Karstark.

695
00:42:32.520 --> 00:42:33.840
Gut him!

696
00:42:46.160 --> 00:42:48.160
Get back! I want his head!

697
00:42:49.600 --> 00:42:51.840
Any man who stands
Between a father

698
00:42:52.000 --> 00:42:54.280
And his vengeance asks for death.

699
00:42:54.440 --> 00:42:56.400
Lord Karstark.

700
00:42:56.560 --> 00:42:59.320
This man is our prisoner.

701
00:42:59.480 --> 00:43:01.080
This monster killed my son.

702
00:43:01.240 --> 00:43:03.120
And crippled mine.

703
00:43:03.280 --> 00:43:04.880
He will answer for his crimes.

704
00:43:05.040 --> 00:43:06.840
I promise you. but not here.

705
00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:09.040
I will have his head.
And if you try and stop me...

706
00:43:09.200 --> 00:43:11.400
You will strike me down?

707
00:43:11.560 --> 00:43:13.680
Have you forgotten me. ser?

708
00:43:13.840 --> 00:43:15.640
I am the widow of your
Liege Lord Eddard Stark.

709
00:43:15.800 --> 00:43:17.200
I am the mother of your king!

710
00:43:17.360 --> 00:43:19.880
-And where is our king now?
-You know very well.

711
00:43:20.040 --> 00:43:22.040
He has gone to the crag
To accept the surrender.

712
00:43:22.200 --> 00:43:25.640
Aye. gone to the crag.
But not to negotiate.

713
00:43:25.800 --> 00:43:27.480
He brought that
Foreign bitch with him.

714
00:43:27.640 --> 00:43:30.320
-How dare you?
-Threatening my lady
Is an act of treason.

715
00:43:30.480 --> 00:43:33.200
Treason? How can it be treason
To kill Lannisters?

716
00:43:33.360 --> 00:43:35.280
I understand your grief. my lord...

717
00:43:35.440 --> 00:43:37.680
Better than most I understand it...

718
00:43:37.840 --> 00:43:40.520
But in the name of my son.
The king in the north.

719
00:43:40.680 --> 00:43:42.320
Stand down.

720
00:43:44.000 --> 00:43:45.760
When your son returns.

721
00:43:45.920 --> 00:43:47.880
I will demand this murderer's head.

722
00:43:48.040 --> 00:43:50.200
Wise men do not
Make demands of kings.

723
00:43:50.360 --> 00:43:53.240
Fathers who love their sons do.

724
00:43:53.400 --> 00:43:55.440
I will have his head.

725
00:43:57.160 --> 00:44:00.760
Thank you for fighting
On my behalf. Lady Stark.

726
00:44:00.920 --> 00:44:02.480
I would have come
To your defense. but...

727
00:44:02.640 --> 00:44:05.080
Take him to the stockades.

728
00:44:05.240 --> 00:44:07.240
Bind him with every chain
You can find!

729
00:44:07.400 --> 00:44:08.760
You've become a real she-wolf
In your later years.

730
00:44:08.920 --> 00:44:10.800
There's not much fish left in you.

731
00:44:10.960 --> 00:44:12.400
And gag him!

732
00:44:16.720 --> 00:44:19.560
Since when do you light
Your own candles?

733
00:44:19.720 --> 00:44:21.840
Since I decided that
I can't stand to look

734
00:44:22.000 --> 00:44:25.080
At any of my handmaidens
For another instant.

735
00:44:26.520 --> 00:44:29.440
How many times can you
Read one raven scroll?

736
00:44:29.600 --> 00:44:33.000
Stannis Baratheon's fleet
Has been spotted sailing north

737
00:44:33.160 --> 00:44:35.640
Past tarth... 200 ships.

738
00:44:35.800 --> 00:44:39.600
-More than we have.
-Yes. that's more than we have.

739
00:44:39.760 --> 00:44:41.880
He'll be at our gates
Within five days.

740
00:44:42.040 --> 00:44:43.600
Four if he has the wind.

741
00:44:43.760 --> 00:44:46.280
We have strong. high walls.

742
00:44:46.440 --> 00:44:49.240
We'll rain fire
Down on them from above.

743
00:44:49.400 --> 00:44:51.360
"rain fire on them from above."

744
00:44:51.520 --> 00:44:53.160
You're quoting father. aren't you?

745
00:44:53.320 --> 00:44:56.400
Why not? He has a good mind
For strategy. doesn't he?

746
00:44:56.560 --> 00:44:59.080
We call it tactics. not strategy.

747
00:44:59.240 --> 00:45:01.120
But. yes. he does have
A good mind for it.

748
00:45:01.280 --> 00:45:02.920
The best mind. some would say.

749
00:45:03.080 --> 00:45:04.800
Sadly. he's not here.

750
00:45:05.760 --> 00:45:08.040
It's just you. me. and Joffrey.

751
00:45:08.200 --> 00:45:10.160
The lord of the seven kingdoms

752
00:45:10.320 --> 00:45:11.800
And protector of the realm.

753
00:45:13.600 --> 00:45:15.200
I'm sure you'll make
A point eventually.

754
00:45:15.360 --> 00:45:18.480
He needs to start acting like a king.

755
00:45:18.640 --> 00:45:21.480
This war you started
Is coming to our doorstep.

756
00:45:21.640 --> 00:45:23.720
And if the entire city
Wants Joffrey dead...

757
00:45:23.880 --> 00:45:26.000
I'm not the one giving
The boy whores to abuse.

758
00:45:26.160 --> 00:45:28.120
I thought the girls might help him.

759
00:45:28.280 --> 00:45:30.280
-Did you?
-I was wrong.

760
00:45:33.040 --> 00:45:35.440
If we can't control him...

761
00:45:35.600 --> 00:45:36.960
Do you think I haven't tried?

762
00:45:39.440 --> 00:45:42.000
He doesn't listen to me.

763
00:45:43.640 --> 00:45:46.640
It's hard to put a leash on a dog

764
00:45:46.800 --> 00:45:49.200
Once you've put
A crown on its head.

765
00:45:52.480 --> 00:45:55.000
I always hoped
He'd be like Jaime.

766
00:45:57.120 --> 00:45:59.120
He looks like him...

767
00:46:02.160 --> 00:46:04.640
In a certain light.

768
00:46:07.080 --> 00:46:08.800
The boy is more Robert than Jaime.

769
00:46:08.960 --> 00:46:12.600
Robert was a drunken fool.
But he didn't enjoy cruelty.

770
00:46:14.640 --> 00:46:17.520
Sometimes I wonder...

771
00:46:17.680 --> 00:46:19.920
What?

772
00:46:20.080 --> 00:46:23.240
If this is the price

773
00:46:23.400 --> 00:46:27.440
For what we've done. for our sins.

774
00:46:27.600 --> 00:46:29.440
Sins?

775
00:46:29.600 --> 00:46:31.040
The Targaryens...

776
00:46:31.200 --> 00:46:34.080
Wed brother and sister
For hundreds of years. I know.

777
00:46:36.240 --> 00:46:39.600
That's what Jaime and I
Would say to each other
In our moments of doubt.

778
00:46:39.760 --> 00:46:43.240
It's what I told Ned Stark
When he was stupid enough
To confront me.

779
00:46:45.320 --> 00:46:48.280
Half the Targaryens
Went mad. didn't they?

780
00:46:48.440 --> 00:46:49.760
What's the saying?

781
00:46:49.920 --> 00:46:54.040
Every time a Targaryen is born.
The gods flip a coin.

782
00:46:54.200 --> 00:46:56.480
You've beaten the odds.

783
00:46:56.640 --> 00:46:58.960
Tommen and Myrcella
Are good. decent children.

784
00:46:59.120 --> 00:47:00.720
Both of them.

785
00:47:02.840 --> 00:47:04.760
( crying )

786
00:47:27.240 --> 00:47:29.840
-Why wait?
-We're sworn to the king.

787
00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:32.600
-There's not a king.
-That's treason.

788
00:47:32.760 --> 00:47:34.600
So is saving Lannisters. yeah?

789
00:47:34.760 --> 00:47:37.400
-Back off. you.
-No. I won't.

790
00:47:37.560 --> 00:47:39.760
Your son returns at dawn. my lady?

791
00:47:39.920 --> 00:47:41.280
So they say.

792
00:47:41.440 --> 00:47:44.160
Brienne:
The Kingslayer won't last the night.

793
00:47:44.320 --> 00:47:47.120
The more they drink.
The angrier they'll get.

794
00:47:47.280 --> 00:47:49.440
And when the Karstarks
Draw their swords...

795
00:47:49.600 --> 00:47:52.640
Who wants to die
Defending a Lannister?

796
00:47:53.680 --> 00:47:55.160
Come.

797
00:48:10.440 --> 00:48:12.920
I need to be alone with him.

798
00:48:13.080 --> 00:48:16.520
-My lady. our orders...
-Your orders. which I just gave you.

799
00:48:16.680 --> 00:48:18.920
Are to leave me alone with him.

800
00:48:23.720 --> 00:48:25.840
Come to say goodbye. Lady Stark?

801
00:48:26.000 --> 00:48:31.960
I believe it's my last night
in this world. Is that a woman?

802
00:48:32.120 --> 00:48:34.600
Do you hear them out there?

803
00:48:34.760 --> 00:48:37.160
They want your head.

804
00:48:37.320 --> 00:48:40.480
Well. old Lord Karstark
Doesn't seem to like me.

805
00:48:40.640 --> 00:48:43.680
You strangled his son
With your chains.

806
00:48:43.840 --> 00:48:45.800
Oh. oh.

807
00:48:45.960 --> 00:48:47.480
Was he the one on guard duty?

808
00:48:47.640 --> 00:48:49.920
( sighs )

809
00:48:50.080 --> 00:48:51.720
He was in my way.

810
00:48:51.880 --> 00:48:53.200
Any knight would have
Done the same.

811
00:48:53.360 --> 00:48:55.400
You are no knight.

812
00:48:55.560 --> 00:48:57.880
You have forsaken
Every vow you ever took.

813
00:48:58.040 --> 00:48:59.680
So many vows.

814
00:48:59.840 --> 00:49:01.520
They make you swear and swear.

815
00:49:01.680 --> 00:49:05.520
Defend the king. obey the king.
Obey your father.

816
00:49:05.680 --> 00:49:08.800
Protect the innocent.
Defend the weak.

817
00:49:08.960 --> 00:49:12.520
But what if your father
Despises the king?

818
00:49:12.680 --> 00:49:15.920
What if the king
Massacres the innocent?

819
00:49:16.080 --> 00:49:18.120
It's too much.

820
00:49:18.280 --> 00:49:21.560
No matter what you do.
You're forsaking one vow or another.

821
00:49:21.720 --> 00:49:24.160
Where did you find this beast?

822
00:49:25.520 --> 00:49:28.280
She is a truer knight
Than you will ever be.

823
00:49:28.440 --> 00:49:30.560
Kingslayer.

824
00:49:30.720 --> 00:49:33.080
Kingslayer.

825
00:49:33.240 --> 00:49:35.440
What a king he was.

826
00:49:35.600 --> 00:49:38.840
Here's to Aerys Targaryen.
The second of his name.

827
00:49:39.000 --> 00:49:42.000
Lord of the seven kingdoms.
Protector of the realm.

828
00:49:42.160 --> 00:49:45.680
And to the sword
I shoved in his back.

829
00:49:47.080 --> 00:49:49.760
You are a man without honor.

830
00:49:51.240 --> 00:49:53.160
Do you know

831
00:49:53.320 --> 00:49:56.360
I've never been with
Any woman but Cersei?

832
00:49:56.520 --> 00:49:59.120
So in my own way.

833
00:49:59.280 --> 00:50:04.000
I have more honor
Than poor old dead Ned.

834
00:50:05.800 --> 00:50:07.840
What was the name
Of that bastard he fathered?

835
00:50:08.000 --> 00:50:11.200
-Brienne.
-No. that wasn't it.

836
00:50:11.360 --> 00:50:15.320
Snow. a bastard from the north.

837
00:50:15.480 --> 00:50:18.000
Now. when... when good old Ned

838
00:50:18.160 --> 00:50:21.320
Came home with some whore's baby.

839
00:50:21.480 --> 00:50:24.480
Did you pretend to love it?

840
00:50:24.640 --> 00:50:28.360
No. You're not very good
At pretending.

841
00:50:28.520 --> 00:50:30.520
You're an honest woman.

842
00:50:30.680 --> 00:50:33.880
You hated that boy. didn't you?

843
00:50:34.040 --> 00:50:36.240
How could you not hate him?

844
00:50:36.400 --> 00:50:38.680
The walking. talking reminder

845
00:50:38.840 --> 00:50:42.200
That the honorable
Lord Eddard Stark

846
00:50:42.360 --> 00:50:44.800
Fucked another woman.

847
00:50:47.120 --> 00:50:49.240
Your sword.

848
00:50:53.640 --> 00:50:56.720
I told you what would happen.

849
00:50:56.880 --> 00:50:58.880
All of you...

850
00:51:00.600 --> 00:51:04.480
I told you what would happen
If you served me loyally...

851
00:51:04.640 --> 00:51:06.840
And what would happen
If you did not.

852
00:51:07.000 --> 00:51:09.560
What are you doing?
What have you done?

853
00:51:09.720 --> 00:51:11.680
If there's any who still question
Whether your new lord

854
00:51:11.840 --> 00:51:13.160
Means what he says...

855
00:51:16.040 --> 00:51:18.720
Here is the answer to your question.

856
00:51:18.880 --> 00:51:21.680
( crowd gasps. murmurs )

857
00:51:27.600 --> 00:51:29.680
No!

858
00:51:39.600 --> 00:51:42.520
( theme music playing )
